/-!
# The completion formula at the adic quotients, from the Koszul tower

Let `(𝒞, 𝒪)` be a ringed site, let `f_1, …, f_r` be global sections of `𝒪` and let
`ℐ = (f_1, …, f_r)` be the ideal sheaf they generate. [Stacks, Tag 0A0E], which is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isDerivedLimit_tensorDerivedDualSystem_koszulPowerSystem_canonical`,
says that the derived completion `K^∧` of [Stacks, Tag 099B] is a derived limit of the tower

`n ↦ K ⊗^𝐋_𝒪 Kₙ^∨`,  `Kₙ = K(𝒪, f_1^{n+1}, …, f_r^{n+1})`.

[Stacks, Tag 099M] replaces that tower by the tower of adic quotients,
`n ↦ K ⊗^𝐋_𝒪 𝒪/ℐⁿ⁺¹`, which is `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.adicReductionTower`. The source
does so by citing [Stacks, Tag 0921]: over a *Noetherian* coefficient ring the pro-systems
`{Kₙ^∨}` and `{Λ/Iⁿ}` of the derived category of the coefficients are isomorphic.

This file carries out that replacement. The pro-isomorphism of the two towers in `D(𝒪)` is a
hypothesis here — it is the one input of the source's proof that this library does not have, and
it is where Noetherianity enters; without some such hypothesis the conclusion is **false**, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_not_isIso_derivedCompletionComparison` ([Stacks, Tag 0CQH]).
Everything else in the source's proof is discharged.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.koszulPowerDualSystem`: the inverse system `n ↦ Kₙ^∨` of the
  derived duals of the Koszul complexes on the positive powers of `f_1, …, f_r`. This is the
  system the source calls `{Kₙ}`, its `Kₙ` being the `𝒪`-dual of the Koszul complex in degrees
  `0, …, r`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.adicQuotientDerivedTower`: the inverse system `n ↦ 𝒪/ℐⁿ⁺¹` of
  adic quotients of the structure sheaf, placed in degree zero of `D(𝒪)`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.koszulPowerDualIsoSheafHomComplex`: the `n`-th term `Kₙ^∨` of the
  dual Koszul tower is the ordinary internal Hom complex `𝑆heafHom_𝒪(K(𝒪, f^{n+1}), 𝒪[0])`, by
  [Stacks, Tag 08JH].

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.proIso_tensor_adicReductionTower`: a pro-isomorphism of the two
  towers of sheaves is carried to one of the towers obtained by derived-tensoring with `K`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isDerivedLimit_adicReductionTower_completionFunctor_of_proIso`:
  **the formula of [Stacks, Tag 099M] from the pro-isomorphism of the two towers.** Granted
  `{Kₙ^∨} ≅ {𝒪/ℐⁿ⁺¹}` as pro-objects of `D(𝒪)`, the derived completion `K^∧` of
  [Stacks, Tag 099B] is a derived limit of `n ↦ K ⊗^𝐋_𝒪 𝒪/ℐⁿ⁺¹`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isDerivedComplete_iff_isDerivedLimit_adicReductionTower_of_proIso`:
  **the criterion of [Stacks, Tag 099M] from the same pro-isomorphism**: `K` is derived complete
  along `ℐ` exactly when it is itself a derived limit of that tower.

## Implementation notes

The `@[stacks 099M]` attribute is deliberately **not** attached: the pro-isomorphism of the two
towers in `D(𝒪)` is carried as a hypothesis, and the source derives it. What is missing for it
is recorded in the module documentation of
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.koszulPowerDualIsoSheafHomComplex` and in the discussion below.

The source states [Stacks, Tag 099M] for the constant ringed site `(𝒞, Λ̲)` of a Noetherian ring
`Λ` and the constant ideal sheaf of `I ⊂ Λ`; the statements here are for an arbitrary ringed site
and the ideal sheaf generated by finitely many global sections, which is where the Koszul tower
of [Stacks, Tag 0A0E] lives. On the constant site the hypothesis is exactly [Stacks, Tag 0921]
transported along the constant sheaf of modules functor
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.Constant.constantModuleSheafFunctor`, which is exact, together with the
identification of `Kₙ^∨` with the constant sheaf of the dual Koszul complex over `Λ` and of
`𝒪/ℐⁿ` with the constant sheaf of `Λ/Iⁿ`.

*What the transport already has.* The constant sheaf of modules functor is exact
(`Stacks.SheafOfModules.Constant.preservesFiniteLimits_constantModuleSheafFunctor` and its
colimit companion) and additive, so `CategoryTheory.Functor.mapDerivedCategory` is the induced
functor on derived categories and `CategoryTheory.Functor.mapDerivedCategorySingleFunctor`
commutes it with the degree-zero placement; the constant ringed site is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.constantRingedSite`, with
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.constantRingSheafIso` identifying its sheaf of rings and
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.constantFunctorOver` the constant sheaf of modules functor over a
slice; and [Stacks, Tag 0921] is available in the shape
`InverseSequence.ProIso.whiskerRight` consumes, as
`NoetherianKoszulProIso.nonempty_proIso_koszulPowerSystem_quotientPowerSystem` in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/FormalGeometry/DerivedCompletionRinged/KoszulQuotientProIso.lean`.

*What is missing.* Four things, none of them a Stacks tag the library lacks.

1. **The dual Koszul complex.** No declaration identifies `Kₙ^∨` with an explicitly constructed
   complex. `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedDualIsoSheafHomComplex` ([Stacks, Tag 08JH])
   lands in the `@[no_expose]` complex `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.sheafHomComplex`, whose
   differentials are therefore not available to be matched with those of a Koszul complex; only
   its terms are, by `Stacks.SheafOfModules.homStructureSheafDegreeIso`. There is a second route
   that does not touch `sheafHomComplex`: `Stacks.SheafOfModules.Strict.dualComplex`
   ([Stacks, Tag 0FPR]) is an explicit complex whose differential is the signed transpose
   (`Stacks.SheafOfModules.Strict.dualComplex_d`) and is a left dual of its source at the
   complex level (`Stacks.SheafOfModules.Strict.exactPairingDualComplex`), while
   `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedDualIsoLeftDual` identifies the derived dual with any
   left dual in `D(𝒪)`. The link those two want is the complex-level exact pairing pushed
   through `DerivedCategory.Q` to a pairing at the derived tensor product of [Stacks, Tag 0FPT],
   and that is done nowhere.
2. **The Koszul complex of constant sheaves.** `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.koszulPowerComplex`
   on the constant site is nowhere identified with the constant sheaf of the Koszul complex over
   `Λ`. Its terms are products of copies of the unit sheaf and its differentials are the
   multiplications `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.koszulScalar`, so this asks only that an exact
   additive functor commute with `AlternatingCech.complex`.
3. **The adic quotients of the constant sheaf.** [Stacks, Tag 093M] is in the library as
   `Stacks.ConstantSheaf.constantSheaf_quotientByIdealAction`, but at a single power, and in
   `Sheaf J (ModuleCat Λ)` rather than in
   `SheafOfModules (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)` where
   `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.adicQuotientTower` lives. Carrying it to every power, to the
   sheaf-theoretic power `ℐⁿ` of `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.idealOfGlobalSections`, and
   across the two models is not done; nor is the pro-isomorphism
   `{Λ/(f_1ⁿ, …, f_rⁿ)} ≅ {Λ/Iⁿ}` that the source uses alongside [Stacks, Tag 0921].
4. **Universes.** `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.constantRingedSite` is built only at
   `RingedSite.{0, 0, 0}`, so even with 1–3 the transport would state [Stacks, Tag 099M] for a
   site in `Type 0` and a coefficient ring in `Type 0`, not for the arbitrary site of the source.

Both towers are tensored with `K` by the same functor,
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.derivedTensorProductFunctor X |>.obj K`, which is the `tensor` field of the
canonical derived tensor product of [Stacks, Tag 06YU]; so the pro-isomorphism of the towers of
sheaves is whiskered into a pro-isomorphism of the towers in `D(𝒪)` by
`InverseSequence.ProIso.whiskerRight`, and [Stacks, Tag 0H9L]
(`Rlim.Pro.nonempty_iso_of_isDerivedLimit_of_pro_isomorphism`) identifies the two derived limits.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 099M](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099M)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A0E](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A0E)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0921](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0921)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0H9L](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0H9L)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CQH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CQH)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 093M](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/093M)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FPR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FPR)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated Opposite

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard
attribute [local instance] AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.hasSheafCompose_forget₂_ringCat

/-- Being a derived limit transports along an isomorphism of the limit object. The general API
has this for an isomorphism of the *system*
(`CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated.IsDerivedLimit.of_iso`) but not for one of the object. -/
private theorem isDerivedLimit_of_objIso {D : Type*} [Category D] [HasZeroObject D]
    [HasShift D ℤ] [Preadditive D] [∀ n : ℤ, (shiftFunctor D n).Additive] [Pretriangulated D]
    {F : ℕᵒᵖ ⥤ D} [HasProduct fun n : ℕ => F.obj ⟨n⟩] {K L : D} (e : K ≅ L)
    (hL : IsDerivedLimit F L) : IsDerivedLimit F K := by
  obtain ⟨p, δ, hT⟩ := hL
  refine ⟨e.hom ≫ p, δ ≫ (shiftFunctor D (1 : ℤ)).map e.inv,
    isomorphic_distinguished _ hT _ (Triangle.isoMk _ _ e (Iso.refl _) (Iso.refl _) ?_ ?_ ?_)⟩ <;>
    simp

section Towers

variable (X : RingedSite.{u, u, u})
  [HasSheafify X.J AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [X.J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]

/-- **The inverse system `n ↦ Kₙ^∨` of the derived duals of the Koszul complexes** on the
positive powers of `f_1, …, f_r`: the opposite of the Koszul system of
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.koszulPowerSystem`, followed by the derived dual
`L ↦ R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(L, 𝒪)` of [Stacks, Tag 08JD].

This is the system the source of [Stacks, Tag 0A0E] and [Stacks, Tag 099M] calls `{Kₙ}`: its
`Kₙ` is the `𝒪`-dual of the Koszul complex in degrees `0, …, r`, and so sits in degrees
`-r, …, 0`. Tensoring it with `K` gives the tower
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.tensorDerivedDualSystem` of [Stacks, Tag 0A0A]. -/
abbrev koszulPowerDualSystem {r : ℕ} [HasWeakSheafify X.J CommRingCat.{u}]
    (f : Fin r → Presheaf.globalSections (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{u})) :
    ℕᵒᵖ ⥤ DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) :=
  (koszulPowerSystem X f ⋙ DerivedCategory.Q).op ⋙
    (derivedSheafHomBifunctor X).flip.obj (derivedStructureSheaf X)

/-- **The tower `n ↦ 𝒪/ℐⁿ⁺¹` of adic quotients of the structure sheaf, in `D(𝒪)`**: the tower of
sheaves `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.adicQuotientTower` placed in degree zero. Tensoring it with
`K` gives `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.adicReductionTower`. -/
abbrev adicQuotientDerivedTower
    (I : SheafOfModules.Submodule
      (SheafOfModules.unit (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) :
    ℕᵒᵖ ⥤ DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) :=
  adicQuotientTower X I ⋙
    DerivedCategory.singleFunctor
      (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) 0

/-- **The `n`-th term of the dual Koszul tower is the ordinary internal Hom complex
`𝑆heafHom_𝒪(K(𝒪, f^{n+1}), 𝒪[0])`.** This is [Stacks, Tag 08JH]
(`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedDualIsoSheafHomComplexOfIsStrictlyPerfect`) applied to the
Koszul complex, which is strictly perfect by
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isStrictlyPerfect_koszulPowerComplex`.

It names the terms of the tower but not its differentials:
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.sheafHomComplex` is `@[no_expose]`, so the differentials of the
representing complex are not available, and this is therefore not an identification of `Kₙ^∨`
with a Koszul complex. -/
def koszulPowerDualIsoSheafHomComplex {r : ℕ} [HasWeakSheafify X.J CommRingCat.{u}]
    [X.J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ RingCat.{u} AddCommGrpCat.{u})]
    (f : Fin r → Presheaf.globalSections (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{u})) (n : ℕ) :
    (koszulPowerDualSystem X f).obj (op n) ≅
      DerivedCategory.Q.obj
        (sheafHomComplex X (koszulPowerComplex X f n) (structureSheafComplex X)).obj :=
  derivedDualIsoSheafHomComplexOfIsStrictlyPerfect X (koszulPowerComplex X f n)
    (isStrictlyPerfect_koszulPowerComplex X f n)

end Towers

section Formula

variable (X : RingedSite.{u, u, u})
  [HasSheafify X.J AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [X.J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ V : X.C, HasSheafify (X.J.over V) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ V : X.C, (X.J.over V).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ V : X.C, (X.J.over V).HasSheafCompose (forget₂ RingCat.{u} AddCommGrpCat.{u})]
  [∀ V : X.C, (X.J.over V).HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{u} RingCat.{u})]
  [(Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, u, u} X.O).Additive]
  [∀ A, ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, u, u} X.O).obj A).Additive]
  [∀ K₁ K₂ : HomologicalComplex
      (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf.{u, u, u} X.O))
      (ComplexShape.up ℤ),
    HomologicalComplex.HasMapBifunctor K₁ K₂ (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor X.O)
      (ComplexShape.up ℤ)]
  {r : ℕ} [HasWeakSheafify X.J CommRingCat.{u}]
  (f : Fin r → Presheaf.globalSections (X.O.obj ⋙ forget CommRingCat.{u}))

/-- **A pro-isomorphism of the dual Koszul tower with the adic quotient tower is carried to one
of the two towers tensored with `K`.** Both towers of [Stacks, Tag 099M] are obtained from towers
of sheaves by the same functor `- ↦ K ⊗^𝐋_𝒪 -`, so this is
`InverseSequence.ProIso.whiskerRight`. -/
def proIso_tensor_adicReductionTower
    (I : SheafOfModules.Submodule
      (SheafOfModules.unit (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))
    (K : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))
    (a : InverseSequence.ProIso (koszulPowerDualSystem X f) (adicQuotientDerivedTower X I)) :
    InverseSequence.ProIso
      (tensorDerivedDualSystem X (Stacks.SheafOfModules.canonicalDerivedTensorProduct.{u} X)
        (koszulPowerSystem X f ⋙ DerivedCategory.Q) K)
      (adicReductionTower X I K) :=
  a.whiskerRight ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.derivedTensorProductFunctor X).obj K)

/-- **The formula of [Stacks, Tag 099M], from the pro-isomorphism of the two towers.** Let
`(𝒞, 𝒪)` be a ringed site, let `f_1, …, f_r` be global sections of `𝒪` and let
`ℐ = (f_1, …, f_r)`. Suppose the inverse system `n ↦ Kₙ^∨` of the duals of the Koszul complexes
on the positive powers of the `f_i` is isomorphic, as a pro-object of `D(𝒪)`, to the tower
`n ↦ 𝒪/ℐⁿ⁺¹`. Then the derived completion `K^∧` of [Stacks, Tag 099B],
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.completionFunctor`, is a derived limit of the tower

`n ↦ K ⊗^𝐋_𝒪 𝒪/ℐⁿ⁺¹`,

the derived tensor product being the canonical one of [Stacks, Tag 06YU].

The pro-isomorphism is the only hypothesis, and it is what the source gets from
[Stacks, Tag 0921] on the constant site of a Noetherian ring. It cannot be dropped: by
[Stacks, Tag 0CQH], `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_not_isIso_derivedCompletionComparison`,
the conclusion fails for some ringed site, some finite-type ideal sheaf and some `K`. -/
theorem isDerivedLimit_adicReductionTower_completionFunctor_of_proIso
    (K : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))
    [HasCoproduct ((koszulPowerSystem X f ⋙ DerivedCategory.Q).obj)]
    (a : InverseSequence.ProIso (koszulPowerDualSystem X f)
      (adicQuotientDerivedTower X (idealOfGlobalSections X f))) :
    IsDerivedLimit (adicReductionTower X (idealOfGlobalSections X f) K)
      ((completionFunctor X f).obj K) := by
  obtain ⟨M, hM⟩ := exists_isDerivedLimit (adicReductionTower X (idealOfGlobalSections X f) K)
  obtain ⟨e⟩ := Rlim.Pro.nonempty_iso_of_isDerivedLimit_of_pro_isomorphism _ _ _ M
    (isDerivedLimit_tensorDerivedDualSystem_koszulPowerSystem_canonical X f K) hM
    (proIso_tensor_adicReductionTower X f (idealOfGlobalSections X f) K a)
  exact isDerivedLimit_of_objIso e hM

/-- **The criterion of [Stacks, Tag 099M], from the pro-isomorphism of the two towers.** Under the
same hypothesis as
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isDerivedLimit_adicReductionTower_completionFunctor_of_proIso`, an
object `K` of `D(𝒪)` is derived complete along `ℐ = (f_1, …, f_r)` exactly when `K` is itself a
derived limit of the tower `n ↦ K ⊗^𝐋_𝒪 𝒪/ℐⁿ⁺¹`.

Both directions go through the formula: if `K` is derived complete then the completion map
`K ⟶ K^∧` is invertible by
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isIso_completionUnit_app_of_isDerivedComplete_idealOfGlobalSections`
([Stacks, Tag 099B]), and if `K` is a derived limit of the tower then `K` is isomorphic to `K^∧`,
derived limits of one system being isomorphic, and `K^∧` is derived complete by
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isDerivedComplete_completionFunctor`. -/
theorem isDerivedComplete_iff_isDerivedLimit_adicReductionTower_of_proIso
    (K : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))
    [HasCoproduct ((koszulPowerSystem X f ⋙ DerivedCategory.Q).obj)]
    (a : InverseSequence.ProIso (koszulPowerDualSystem X f)
      (adicQuotientDerivedTower X (idealOfGlobalSections X f))) :
    IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} X (idealOfGlobalSections X f) K ↔
      IsDerivedLimit (adicReductionTower X (idealOfGlobalSections X f) K) K := by
  have hcompl := isDerivedLimit_adicReductionTower_completionFunctor_of_proIso X f K a
  refine ⟨fun hK ↦ ?_, fun hK ↦ ?_⟩
  · have := isIso_completionUnit_app_of_isDerivedComplete_idealOfGlobalSections X f K hK
    exact isDerivedLimit_of_objIso (asIso ((completionUnit X f).app K)) hcompl
  · obtain ⟨e⟩ := Rlim.Pro.nonempty_iso_of_isDerivedLimit_of_pro_isomorphism _ _ _ K
      hcompl hK (InverseSequence.ProIso.ofNatIso (Iso.refl _))
    exact (isDerivedComplete_iff_of_iso X (idealOfGlobalSections X f) e).1
      (isDerivedComplete_completionFunctor X f K)

end Formula

end AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

end
